{"id": "EUVD-2026-104299", "enisaUuid": "626f9429-d894-309e-8ce8-a18c345554cc", "description": "libtins through 4.6 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in DNS::soa_record::init that allows remote attackers to read past buffer bounds by supplying SOA data lacking NUL terminators. Attackers can feed raw SOA RDATA without a zero byte to applications using the buffer constructor, causing strlen to overrun the heap buffer and possibly crash.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T17:57:12", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libtins-dns-name-parsing-oob-read", "https://github.com/mfontanini/libtins/blob/v4.6/src/dns.cpp#L698-L710", "https://github.com/mfontanini/libtins", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libtins-through-4.6-out-of-bounds-read-via-dns-soa-record-init"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112274", "GHSA-4c37-573g-qpf9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "54da97bc-a914-38a7-8e5b-31afbe0c93ba", "product": {"name": "libtins", "vendor": {"name": "libtins"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ff916c4e-9679-36b2-aee4-e307fd0a13c3", "vendor": {"name": "libtins"}}], "isExploited": false}